member.summary:
Reduces a construct snippet to its syntactic skeleton: the normalizedConstructShape of §D.2. Rules, applied in order:
absolute file paths (any run/work/temp root, Windows drive/UNC or Unix) → lit (issue #1750:
neutralizes run-scoped paths regardless of prefix, before anything else can tokenize them);
string/char/interpolated literals → lit;
numeric literals → lit;
identifiers and keywords → id (strips all names);
runs of whitespace → a single space; trim ends.
Punctuation/operators/brackets are preserved as the structural skeleton. The result keeps the <i>shape</i> (e.g. id id[id] = id(id, lit)) while erasing the names, numbers, paths, and positions that vary per occurrence, run, or machine.
